SUMMARY:
- `Server::ClientConnection::serve()` is the main per-client loop for a chat-like protocol.
- On connect, it sends a long welcome banner mentioning:
  - “Humm_s interpreter”
  - users online / PMs
  - “Send your programs @System!!”
  - re-log or `/help`
- It then iterates over all current client connections and sends their presence to the new client via `sendSystemMessage(..., 2)`.
- It also sends and broadcasts `"Anonomnomnom"` as a system message, then sets the client’s displayed name/string to `"Anonomnomnom"`.

Protocol framing:
- Loop does `recv(fd, &local_22, 1, 0x42)` then `recv(fd, &local_21, 1, 0)`.
- If first `recv` returns 0: marks connection dead and returns.
- The second byte (`local_21`) controls message type / delimiter behavior.
- Valid start/type bytes are: `0x01`, `0x02`, `0x06`, `'*'` (`0x2a`).
- End-of-message marker is `0x03`.
- While accumulating a message, bytes are appended to `local_a8` only when `bVar3 == true`.

Handlers when delimiter `0x03` is seen:
- If current type == `1`:
  - `broadcastMessage(in_RDI, local_a8, 1, 0)`
  - clears `local_a8`
- If current type == `2`:
  - `sendSystemMessage(in_RDI, local_a8, 1)`
  - builds `<current_name>...<local_a8>` and broadcasts it via `broadcastSystemMessage(..., 3)`
  - then parses `local_a8` to derive a new name:
    - starts from empty string
    - for each char in `local_a8`:
      - if char is space: reset temp string to `""`
      - else append char
    - final temp becomes substring after the last space
  - assigns that result to the client’s name
  - clears `local_a8`
- If current type == `6`:
  - splits `local_a8` at the first space-like transition:
    - chars before first space go to recipient string (`local_68`)
    - remaining non-space chars go to message string (`local_48`)
  - calls `PM(in_RDI, recipient, message, 1)`
  - clears `local_a8`
- If current type == `'*'` / `0x2a`:
  - calls `hummusInterpreter((basic_string *)in_RDI)`
  - clears `local_a8`
- Otherwise:
  - sends `Bad message. Error code <local_dc>...`
  - clears `local_a8`

Important parsing behavior:
- A byte becomes the active message type only when the newly read byte is one of `{0x01, 0x02, 0x06, '*'}`
  and the code sets:
  - `local_dc = local_21`
  - `bVar3 = true`
- Any other non-delimiter byte while `bVar3` is true gets appended to `local_a8`.
- `usleep(100)` occurs each loop iteration.

Likely command meanings:
- `0x01`: public chat/broadcast
- `0x02`: system/name-related command; also updates nickname to the last space-separated token
- `0x06`: PM; first token = recipient, rest = message
- `'*'`: invoke `hummusInterpreter`

Potentially useful observations from decompilation:
- The interpreter entrypoint is directly reachable by sending type `'*'` followed by payload, then `0x03`.
- Name update logic for type `2` keeps only text after the last space.
- PM parser for type `6` concatenates all non-space chars after the first space into the message.
- `hummusInterpreter` is called with `(basic_string *)in_RDI`, i.e. likely on the client object / embedded current string state rather than explicitly passing `local_a8`.
- There is stack canary protection in this function.
